error[V0307]: this loop's head reads `seen`, so `seen` cannot be changed inside it
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0307_for_head_capture_changed/main.vr:5:9
  |
4 |     for w in words.iter().filter(|w| !seen.contains(w)) {
  |              ------------------------------------------ the loop goes over this until it ends
5 |         seen.push(w.clone());
  |         ^^^^ this loop's head reads `seen`, so `seen` cannot be changed inside it
  |
  = note: in Rust terms, the `for` loop keeps its iterator, and every borrow its closures and arguments hold, until it ends, and a value cannot be changed while it is borrowed
